# Line endings.
#
# The project is built and run on Linux (dev container, WSL, CI) but is also
# checked out on Windows.  With core.autocrlf=true Git converts text files to
# CRLF on checkout, and a shell script with CRLF endings does not run under
# Linux bash ("bash\r: No such file or directory").  The rules below keep the
# files that Linux executes in LF on every platform.

# Store text files with LF in the repository, whatever the platform.
* text=auto

# Executed by bash inside Linux: always LF in the working tree too.
*.sh        text eol=lf
/run        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
# Started as ./menu.py: with CRLF its "#!/usr/bin/env python3" line fails on Linux.
/menu.py    text eol=lf

# Never touch binary files.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.npz   binary
*.so    binary
*.pyd   binary
